               <death when="1823-08-08"> 
                  <placeName>Dublin</placeName></death>
               <occupation>Antiquary</occupation>
               <note type="editorial">
                  <p>Edward Ledwich DNB 1739-1823</p>
                  <p>Edward Ledwich lived mostly in Ireland. However, he spent time in London and in 1791 had joined the Whig Club of Gerrard Street, giving a London address. He was a Fellow of the Society of Antiquaries, alongside <persName key="NOR04">Northmore</persName> who he was often with when Godwin saw him.  </p>
               </note>
